 whose `from` is a proper prefix of its `path`.
 
+### JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a [JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386) —
+a partial JSON document describing the changes to make — to a target JSON document and returns the
+merged document. It never mutates `target`, `patch`, or any value reachable from either.
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+const target = { name: 'Alice', role: 'admin' };
+
+applyMergePatch(target, { role: 'member', nickname: null });
+// => { name: 'Alice', role: 'member' }, and `target` is unchanged
+```
+
+A `null` value in `patch` removes the corresponding member of `target`; an object value is merged
+into it recursively; any other value — including an array — replaces it wholesale. If `patch` itself
+is not an object, it replaces `target` entirely.
+
 ## Development
 
 - `npm test` runs the test suite.
